  "notes": "USAGE:\nOften implies a question meant to provoke thought rather than simply seeking factual information. Common in intellectual, philosophical, and media contexts. The form {問|と}いかけ is used as a noun meaning \"a question\" or \"an inquiry.\"\n\nIchidan verb ({一段動詞|いちだんどうし}).\n- Negative: {問|と}いかけない\n- Polite: {問|と}いかけます\n- Te-form: {問|と}いかけて\n- Past: {問|と}いかけた\n- Noun form: {問|と}いかけ\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {自分|じぶん}に{問|と}いかける: to ask oneself\n- {社会|しゃかい}に{問|と}いかける: to pose a question to society\n- {意味|いみ}を{問|と}いかける: to question the meaning of",
